From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 22:49:15 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Start the mini's macOS state lane for hermes_state's
 load-time imports

hermes_state* imports 17 first-party modules at load time (hermes_constants,
hermes_cli/timefmt, hermes_startup_watchdog, agent/context_compressor, ...).
A change to one alone did not select the PR lane, though a break there fails
`import hermes_state` on the mini (#1538 review notes 4/5).

classify_changes.HERMES_STATE_IMPORTS lists them and joins _HERMES_STATE_PATHS.
The new tests/ci/test_macos_state_import_surface.py reads the imports from the
source with ast (module level, try/else/class bodies; not function-local imports
or `if TYPE_CHECKING:`) and fails until the list equals them, so a new import
must be added and a dropped one removed. Their own imports stay out: the
transitive closure is 182 files and would start the lane on far more PRs; the
4-hourly schedule (now carded on failure by ci_main_watch) covers main for the
rest.

Main pushes no longer start the standalone lane (e1ebb6dc94), so no workflow
push.paths change is needed; this only widens PR selection.

RED (constant empty, no routing): 18 failed (17 modules + exact-list test).
GREEN: CI-routing tests pass. Mutants caught: drop a module from the classifier,
or add a new import to hermes_state.py.

Card: t_01a1d05e8be13a6a
